# DAA-MOODLE

## Design and Analysis of Algorithms

This repository contains organized learning materials and practice problems related to **Design and Analysis of Algorithms (DAA)**. It is intended to support algorithm learning, problem-solving practice, and preparation for academic assessments.

## Topics Covered

- **Time Complexity:** Analysis of algorithm efficiency, time complexity, and space complexity.
- **Greedy Algorithms:** Problem-solving techniques that make locally optimal choices at each step.
- **Divide and Conquer:** Algorithms that divide problems into smaller subproblems, solve them, and combine the results.
- **Dynamic Programming:** Techniques for solving problems using overlapping subproblems and stored results.
- **Competitive Programming:** Practice problems that improve logical thinking, coding skills, and algorithmic problem-solving.

## Repository Structure

```text
DAA-MOODLE/
├── My-Project/
│   ├── TimeComplexity/
│   ├── Greedy/
│   ├── DivideAndConquer/
│   ├── DynamicProgramming/
│   └── CompetitiveProgramming/
└── README.md
```

## Objectives

- Understand fundamental algorithm design techniques.
- Practice solving algorithmic problems.
- Learn to analyze time and space complexity.
- Organize study resources by algorithmic topic.
- Improve problem-solving and programming skills.

## Technologies and Tools

- Git and GitHub for version control and resource management.
- Programming languages and algorithmic techniques as required by individual problems.

## Contribution

Learning resources, problem statements, explanations, and solutions can be added to the appropriate topic folders to keep the repository organized and useful.

---

**Purpose:** A structured collection of resources for learning and practicing Design and Analysis of Algorithms.
